[1.733,"m","Deploy (--mode assisted): ov prints the commands and runs nothing"]
[1.733,"o","$ "]
[1.734,"o","ov stack deploy openvidu-e2e-gcp-ce-s125447 --cloud gcp --gcp-project \"$GCP_PROJECT_ID\" --edition community --certificate-type selfsigned --mode assisted\r\n"]
[7.528,"o","note: recorded this stack's infrastructure in openvidu-stack.yml, so the command that continues this deploy needs no flags\r\n"]
[7.529,"o","── PLAN · nothing below has run ───────────────────────────────────────\r\nRun these commands yourself in your Google Cloud project *** (region europe-west2, zone europe-west2-b); ov runs none of them.\r\nOnce they have finished, run this same command again: ov finds the machines and ends the deploy.\r\n\r\n  # The template, rendered from the one embedded in this CLI for the single node topology,\r\n  # and its variables, written out for you to read (the variables file is 0600: it\r\n  # can carry secrets, such as Meet's seed credentials or a private key):\r\n  #   .openvidu/gcp/tf-gpc-openvidu-singlenode.tf\r\n  #   .openvidu/gcp/openvidu.auto.tfvars.json\r\n  terraform -chdir=.openvidu/gcp init -input=false -no-color -force-copy\r\n  # If this stack already exists, read first what the apply would change: a new startup script\r\n  # (the domain, the certificate, the Meet credentials or another OpenVidu CLI) REPLACES\r\n  # the machine that runs it, which starts again from scratch, and Terraform's plan says \"must be replaced\":\r\n  terraform -chdir=.openvidu/gcp plan\r\n  # Create the machine. deployedBy=instance: it installs OpenVidu on itself with the\r\n  # OpenVidu CLI. `apply` returns when Terraform is done (about 2 minutes, then OpenVidu installs); OpenVidu comes up after.\r\n  terraform -chdir=.openvidu/gcp apply -auto-approve -input=false -no-color\r\n\r\n  # Read back where the stack is (sensitive outputs, such as a generated SSH key, show as\r\n  # <sensitive>: `terraform output -raw <name>` prints one).\r\n  terraform -chdir=.openvidu/gcp output\r\n  # What the stack published: URL and credentials, as Secret Manager secrets under the prefix the stack outputs (OPENVIDU_URL appears once\r\n  # OpenVidu serves: until then this read fails, and ov waits for it).\r\n  PREFIX=\"$(terraform -chdir=.openvidu/gcp output -raw secret_prefix)\"\r\n  gcloud secrets versions access latest --secret=${PREFIX}OPENVIDU_URL --project=***\r\n\r\nNothing above has been run. Once these commands have finished, run this same command again:\r\n\r\n  ov stack deploy openvidu-e2e-gcp-ce-s125447 --cloud gcp --mode assisted\r\n\r\nIt finds the machines, waits for OpenVidu to come up and registers this directory as the\r\nstack. It creates nothing in your account.\r\n── end of plan ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n"]
[7.706,"m","The runbook's commands, exactly as ov printed them 1/6"]
